dummy-x11 (1.0-8) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix: xcb_connection_has_error now uses STATEFUL override — returns 0x5
    (XCB_CONN_CLOSED_PARSE_ERR) on first call only, then returns 0.
    Previous approach (delegating to real libxcb) returned 0x5 on ALL calls,
    causing Chromium to loop 200+ times across 3 processes without switching
    to Wayland. Stateful override ensures Ready() returns false once → browser
    switches to Wayland immediately.
  * New log function: log_exit_int for int-returning functions.
  * New override template: HAS_ERROR_OVERRIDE_TEMPLATE (separate from
    OVERRIDE_TEMPLATE which returns void*).

  -- crick Debian Backports <backports@users.noreply.github.com>  Sun, 25 Oct 2026 08:30:00 +0000

dummy-x11 (1.0-7) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix: xcb_connection_has_error, xcb_connect, and
    xcb_connect_to_display_with_auth_info are now DELEGATED to real libxcb
    instead of being overridden with fake values. Root cause of the 200+ has_error
    loop: overriding xcb_connection_has_error with a hardcoded return value breaks
    Chromium's error detection. Chromium's Connection::XcbConnection() checks
    io_error_handler_ && has_error — io_error_handler_ is a OnceCallback that fires
    once (_exit), then becomes null, leaving 200+ subsequent has_error calls
    unchecked. By delegating to real libxcb, the browser gets a REAL connection
    object with real internal error state; Ready() returns false once, browser
    immediately switches to Wayland (rev 3 behavior: 5 calls total).
  * Remaining overrides: xcb_generate_id (0xffffffff), xcb_flush (0),
    xcb_disconnect (0) — safe values for broken-connection cleanup.
  * Reverted: 0x3 override (was XCB_CONN_CLOSED_MEM_INSUFFICIENT, transient)
    and 0x5 override (was XCB_CONN_CLOSED_PARSE_ERR, but overriding breaks detection).

  -- crick Debian Backports <backports@users.noreply.github.com>  Fri, 25 Oct 2026 07:50:00 +0000

dummy-x11 (1.0-6) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix xcb_connection_has_error override: changed return value from 0x3
    (XCB_CONN_CLOSED_MEM_INSUFFICIENT — transient, browser retries 200+ times)
    to 0x5 (XCB_CONN_CLOSED_PARSE_ERR — permanent fatal). With 0x3 the browser
    never switched to Wayland despite 6 overridden functions. 0x5 is the same
    value real libxcb returns when no X server is available — forces immediate
    fallback to Wayland.
  * README.md and debian/control updated with corrected XCB enum names.

  -- crick Debian Backports <backports@users.none.github.com>  Fri, 24 Oct 2026 19:00:00 +0000

dummy-x11 (1.0-5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Override xcb_connect, xcb_connect_to_display_with_auth_info,
    xcb_generate_id, xcb_flush, xcb_disconnect to return hardcoded values
    instead of delegating to real libxcb. Browser calls has_error 200+
    times but doesn't switch to Wayland when only has_error is overridden.
    Now all called functions return stub values without touching real libxcb.
  * STUB_OVERRIDES expanded from 1 to 6 entries.

  -- crick Debian Backports <backports@users.noreply.github.com>  Fri, 24 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000

dummy-x11 (1.0-4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * xcb_connection_has_error overridden to return XCB_CONN_SERVER_UNAVAILABLE
    (0x3) instead of delegating to real libxcb (which returns
    XCB_CONN_WAITING_FOR_SETUP, 0x5). This forces Yandex Browser to fall back
    from X11 to Wayland.
  * Log file opened in append mode ("a") instead of truncate ("w") to prevent
    log entries from being lost when multiple processes use the stub.
  * README.md and dummy-x11-report updated with override documentation.

  -- crick Debian Backports <backports@users.noreply.github.com>  Fri, 24 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000

dummy-x11 (1.0-3) unstable; urgency=low

  * libxcb.so.1 replaced with a logging wrapper that delegates to the real
    libxcb via dlopen/dlysm. Logs all xcb_* calls to
    /tmp/dummy-x11-libxcb.log (override: $YABROWSER_XCB_LOG).
  * Real libxcb installed at hidden path for delegation.
  * dummy-x11-report updated: libxcb treated as stub, not real.
  * README.md updated with logging details.

